      <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
      <h2 class="section-title" id="about-title">About me</h2>
      <p>I build environmental data that stands up to audit. I've worked on all three sides of carbon measurement: developing the measurement models during my Ph.D., building a digital MRV system at a startup, and now turning carbon methodologies into software inside a standard-setter.</p>
      <p>Today at Verra I work where standards meet software: turning carbon methodologies into digital systems and connecting remote-sensing data providers to the registry. I'm most interested in how AI and Earth observation can make environmental claims of every kind trustworthy. My base is nature-based carbon markets, and I'm extending that work into supply-chain (Scope 3) emissions and broader environmental intelligence.</p>
      <p>Before Verra, I built the data foundations at Virginia Tech: a Ph.D. in geospatial and environmental analysis using LiDAR, satellite imagery and machine learning. Alongside it, I helped build a digital MRV system for Bangladesh's first carbon credit marketplace.</p>
      <p>It all started in Bangladesh's development sector, where I managed sanitation, waste and urban programs with municipalities and NGOs. That work taught me that environmental decisions are only as good as the data behind them. I've since worked across Bangladesh, India, Nepal, Indonesia and the United States.</p>
